infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Self-host vs managed: the crossover is traffic shape
  desc Decompose first — steady load repatriates well, spiky low-floor load does not
  compares
    - label Self-host VMs + commodity CDN — wins on steady load
      children
        - label ~10-15% of the managed bill at steady load
          desc Flat-capacity-shaped traffic — e.g. a sustained 80 req/s with bounded spikes — on a pair of VMs plus a commodity CDN.
        - label Repatriate the image line first
          desc sharp on your own CPU behind CDN caching is usually the single biggest line you can move off the managed platform.
        - label You pay to run the fleet
          desc Idle capacity is cheap here, but operating the servers is the offsetting cost the decomposition has to clear.
    - label Managed platform per-request pricing — wins on spikes
      children
        - label Spiky, low-floor traffic inverts the math
          desc Per-request pricing beats paying for idle capacity when load is bursty with a low floor.
        - label No fleet to operate
          desc The operational cost of running your own servers would eat the self-host savings.
        - label Dynamic routes bill a multiple
          desc A dynamic /pricing route at 1M req/mo (~0.48 GB-s each) lands at a multiple of raw infra rates.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
